      ":question/id": "63d3f39d-4a1c-5646-9607-234dd8196589",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix $A$ below. Which set of entries should be replaced by $0$ to obtain row echelon form **using the fewest replacements**? Leave all other entries unchanged.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 4 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The minimum set is $a_{42}$ and $a_{43}$. Replace these 2 entries with $0$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 4 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\longrightarrow\\,\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 4 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe nonzero rows have leading entries in columns 1, 3, 4, in strictly increasing order, and all zero rows are at the bottom. Each listed removal is necessary: restoring any one of these entries violates a row echelon condition. Checking the possible leading columns shows that fewer than 2 replacements cannot produce row echelon form. Entries to the right of a leading entry may remain nonzero.",
